 "response": "Tepi's budget is now **$1,767K**. Hand tally over about 1,600 records; one missed withdrawal (#0922) was caught and corrected partway, so a recount is worth doing if exactness matters.\n\n**Approach**\n1. Only Finance Office entries change the budget. All other messages were ignored.\n2. I traced each chain of withdrawals back from its latest link. A withdrawal counts only if nothing still in force withdrew it.\n3. Starting from the $1,810K set in #0001, I applied every budget change that was not withdrawn, in record order.\n\n**Example withdrawal chains**\n- **#0002:** #1184 withdraws #0545, which reinstates the withdrawal of #0031. That keeps #0018 in force, which cancels #0005. So #0002 (\u2212$138K) still applies.\n- **#0675:** #0922 withdraws it and is never itself withdrawn. So #0675 (+$264K) does not apply.\n- **#0035:** #0920 withdraws #0331, which keeps #0176 in force. The alternating chain then ends with #0078 in force, which cancels #0069. So #0035 (+$593K) applies.\n\nANSWER: $1767K",
